          'Water management depends entirely on concealed components (sill pan, head flashing, jamb sealant); failure of any concealed element leads to hidden water intrusion that may not be detected until damage is advanced.',
          'Cladding materials that expand or contract (vinyl, fiber cement) can open gaps at flush terminations; thermal movement must be accommodated with engineered joints rather than trim overlap.'
