    content: 'Half-height tile has an undeserved reputation as the budget compromise. In practice, the perception of a half-height installation depends almost entirely on one detail: the termination edge.\n\nA raw tile edge at 48 inches — cut and unfinished — reads as incomplete. A Schluter Jolly or Rondec metal profile at the same height reads as a deliberate architectural choice. The material cost difference is $2–$4 per linear foot. The perceptual difference is enormous.\n\nDesigners specifying half-height tile should coordinate the edge profile with the tile format and grout color before installation begins. The edge height should also align with horizontal fixture lines — mirror bottom, towel bar, vanity light — so the transition feels integrated rather than arbitrary. When these details are coordinated, half-height tile holds its own against full-height in design quality.',
